  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnerships for Green Investment (PAGI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN)):  The ASEAN agriculture, forestry and land use (AFOLU).sector is crucial for the region&apos;s economic growth, food security, climate.change mitigation, and environmental protection. However, agricultural.expansion has led to deforestation, greenhouse gas emissions, and biodiversity.loss, while the sector remains vulnerable to climate hazards. USAID aims to.transition the AFOLU sector towards sustainable, resilient and inclusive.growth, in line with the Indo-Pacific Strategy and ASEAN&apos;s Strategy for Carbon.Neutrality. USAID PAGI will support ASEAN in operationalizing the Action Plan.on Sustainable Agriculture by promoting low-carbon farming, agroforestry and.regenerative agriculture in key crops (e.g., rice, rubber, coffee, coconut)..This will be achieved through public-private-community partnerships,.development of carbon-offset projects and credible standards to create carbon market.opportunities. USAID will scale innovative practices, foster collaborative.platforms for innovation and knowledge exchange. Meanwhile, ASEAN&apos;s.persistent haze pollution caused by forest fires, land clearing, and.agricultural residue burning affect over 70 million people. This underscores.the urgent need to operationalize the ASEAN Investment Framework for.Transboundary Haze. USAID PAGI will build a pipeline of investment-ready.projects and strengthen the capacity of ASEAN and regional stakeholders to mobilize.financing, implement, and monitor sustainable land-use projects aimed at.eliminating transboundary haze. Expected outcomes include a more sustainable.agriculture and commodity sector in ASEAN, free from contributing to haze,.equitable transition for indigenous peoples and local communities to enhance.their welfare through haze-free sustainable agriculture and land management,.and the halting of forest and peatland degradation due to fires by.2030. Assistance to ASEAN will support all member states including high-income.countries of Brun</narrative>
  </description>
